Professional education curriculum
Key industry leaders and academic experts guide the creation of our University of California-approved curricula. Each course is packed with practical information that students can put into practice in real-time. It's designed to provide identified, in-demand job skills that link to regional needs. Courses build upon each other, allowing students to master desired skills in a short program or take a deep dive into an industry. Under the mentoring eye of instructors who are working professionals, students achieve a marked level of professionalism.
Flexible learning paths
We value practical, flexible, and focused learning environments. Join us on campus in Santa Clara in our flexible classrooms (which allows you to stay remote if you choose), or study online. By offering primarily evening, weekend, blended hybrid, and online courses, students enjoy hands-on and collaborative study with instructors working in the top companies in the regions. Like our onsite courses, the flexible format fulfills the F-1 visa requirements for international students.
